    distanceLabel: 'Approximately 7 tidal river miles', paddleTime: '3–6 hours depending on tide, wind, current, shallow sections, traffic, breaks, and landing conditions', summary: 'A bounded Cohansey River tidal planning reach connecting the public Bridgeton municipal ramp with the NJDEP-listed Back Neck wetland-restoration boat site.', statusText: 'Planning route only. NJDEP’s current public-access inventory identifies both endpoints as public Fishing, Boat sites; its official ramp guide warns that the Back Neck Cohansey ramp may lack adequate depth at low tide. Use USGS 01412800 as clearly labeled same-river discharge proxy context, USGS 01413038 as nearby tidal-elevation context, and current tide, wind, water quality, visual depth, and landing checks. No numeric recreational cutoff is transferred.', gaugeSiteId: '01412800', gaugeSiteName: 'Cohansey River at Seeley, NJ', gaugeKind: 'proxy', thresholdSource: { label: 'NJDEP public-access inventory and official Cohansey boat-ramp guide', url: cohanseyRampGuideUrl, provider: 'local' }, routeType: 'recreational', difficulty: 'moderate', riskLevel: 'caution', hazards: ['low_water', 'fast_rise', 'cold_water', 'strainers', 'private_banks', 'urban_water_quality', 'access_uncertain'], safetyNotes: ['Wear a properly fitted PFD continuously, carry communication and rescue gear, and do not paddle beyond the group’s moving-water skills.', 'This is a tidal reach: forecast tide and wind, expect current reversal, shallow mud and shoals, and do not convert a discharge or tide reading into a local safe-depth cutoff. Plan a daylight tide window with margin for a failed landing.', 'The Cohansey passes through developed, marsh, and industrial-adjacent settings. Watch for strainers, floating debris, bridge and dock hydraulics, motorboat traffic, eroding banks, and water-quality advisories; do not use private docks or banks as emergency access.', 'The Bridgeton and Back Neck endpoints are hard route boundaries. Turn around or use a separately verified access if the channel, waterline, landing, or tide window is not safe.'], shuttle: 'Stage at the Back Neck site only after confirming current public access, parking, carry, waterline, tide window, and paddlecraft take-out; then launch at the Bridgeton Municipal Ramp. Do not use bridge shoulders, private marinas, visual-only access points, or unmarked marsh banks as shuttle or bailout access.', permits: 'Follow current NJDEP public-access and water-quality notices, Bridgeton and Fairfield Township rules, New Jersey boating/PFD requirements, tide and weather guidance, and any closure or ramp-maintenance notice. The NJDEP inventory and dated ramp guide do not guarantee a current independent paddle launch or clear landing.', camping: 'No on-route camping is identified. Public ramps, wetland-restoration sites, and tidal shoreline do not grant overnight camping or parking rights; use separately managed lodging or a lawful designated campground.', campingClassification: 'nearby_basecamp', accessCaveats: ['NJDEP’s current access layer identifies BRIC01315 and FT02517 as public Fishing, Boat sites with coordinates and shoreline settings, but the records are access inventory rather than a current ramp survey; verify both sites on launch day.', 'The dated NJDEP ramp guide specifically warns that the Back Neck Cohansey ramp may not have adequate depth at low tide. Do not treat a historical ramp listing as proof of current depth, maintenance, or independent paddlecraft permission.', 'The route ends before the lower Cohansey and Delaware Bay transition. Do not extend into Greenwich marinas, private docks, Delaware Bay, or unreviewed tributaries without a separate tidal-navigation and access review.'], watchFor: ['USGS 01412800 same-river discharge proxy at Seeley, USGS 01413038 Greenwich tidal-elevation context, NOAA tide, wind, recent rain, water quality, and visual depth', 'low-tide mud/shoals, reversing current, shallow water, strainers, floating debris, bridge/dock hydraulics, motorboat traffic, cold-water immersion, and eroding banks', 'Bridgeton and Back Neck parking, ramp condition, carry, waterline, tide window, daylight, closures, and shuttle failure'], evidenceNotes: [{ label: 'Named moving-water corridor', value: 'Cohansey River tidal reach from Bridgeton to the Back Neck wetland-restoration site', note: 'NJDEP’s public-access inventory names both endpoints on the Cohansey River, and the official boat-ramp guide provides route-specific low-tide depth context. The route is bounded before the lower Greenwich/Delaware Bay transition.', sourceUrl: cohanseyAccessUrl }, { label: 'Public endpoint evidence', value: 'BRIC01315 Bridgeton Municipal Ramp and FT02517 Cohansey River Watershed Wetland Restoration Site', note: 'Both current NJDEP inventory records are public Fishing, Boat sites with parking/shoreline fields; current ramp, carry, waterline, and paddlecraft use remain launch gates.', sourceUrl: cohanseyAccessUrl }, { label: 'On/near-water coordinate evidence', value: 'Current NJDEP public-access coordinates for W Broad Street/S Laurel Street and Back Neck Road', note: 'These are official access-area anchors, not surveyed wetted-edge points. Preserve the named access controls and verify exact landing conditions before unloading.', sourceUrl: cohanseyAccessUrl }, { label: 'Proxy flow and tidal evidence', value: 'USGS 01412800 Cohansey River at Seeley, clearly labeled same-river discharge proxy, plus USGS 01413038 Greenwich tidal elevation', note: 'The Seeley station provides route-context discharge history/current availability, while Greenwich provides nearby tidal-elevation context. Use both with NOAA tide, wind, water quality, and visual scouting; no recreational cutoff is inferred.', sourceUrl: cohanseyGaugeUrl }, { label: 'Route-specific low-tide guidance', value: 'NJDEP Cohansey River boat-ramp guide', note: 'The official guide says the Back Neck Cohansey concrete ramp may not have adequate depth at low tide; the warning is retained as a hard planning gate.', sourceUrl: cohanseyRampGuideUrl }, { label: 'Camping posture', value: 'Nearby basecamp only', note: 'No public launch or tidal shoreline camping entitlement is claimed.', sourceUrl: cohanseyRampGuideUrl }], sourceLinks: [{ label: 'NJDEP current public-access inventory layer', url: cohanseyAccessUrl, provider: 'local' }, { label: 'NJDEP Cohansey boat-ramp guide', url: cohanseyRampGuideUrl, provider: 'local' }, { label: 'USGS Cohansey River at Seeley', url: cohanseyGaugeUrl, provider: 'usgs' }, { label: 'USGS Cohansey River at Greenwich tidal station', url: cohanseyTideGaugeUrl, provider: 'usgs' }, { label: 'USGS Cohansey/Maurice tidal-reach study', url: cohanseyResearchUrl, provider: 'usgs' }], contextImageUrl: cohanseyImage, contextImageNote: 'Approved USGS Cohansey River tidal-reach map from Scientific Investigations Report 2025-5090; it provides authoritative same-river route context and does not depict either launch, current tide, waterline, or safety conditions.',
